---
import SocialIcons from "../components/SocialIcons.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  name: SITE.name,
  url: SITE.url,
  email: SITE.email,
  jobTitle: SITE.role,
  worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: SITE.employer },
  sameAs: [SITE.youtube, SITE.github, SITE.linkedin],
};
---

<PageLayout
  title="About"
  description="Backend engineer at Jio Platforms. Public CS course on YouTube. Mumbai."
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />

  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="section-kicker">About</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-5">{SITE.name}</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-sm text-accent">{SITE.tagline}</p>
    <div class="rule-cyan mt-5"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap grid min-w-0 gap-10 pb-16 md:pb-20 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_17.5rem] lg:gap-14">
    <div class="max-w-[42rem] min-w-0 space-y-6 text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <p class="text-ink">
        Backend engineer at Jio Platforms (Jio Cloud / India AI), Mumbai. Java, Spring Boot, distributed systems. A bit over two and a half years in.
      </p>
      <p>
        Day job is infrastructure that has to fail in the right place: quota checks before provision, queues that do not block the caller, replication with a recovery path you can name.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the side I am filming a public CS course. Whiteboard, then interview problems, then a small project you can run. YouTube is the class. Notes will live here when they are ready.
      </p>

      <h2 class="title pt-4 text-ink">Jio Platforms</h2>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-faint">Software Development Engineer I · Dec 2023 to present</p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-accent">
        <li>
          Quota validation framework for Jio Cloud across ROS, HCI, GCP, and internal IaaS. Logical and physical checks before provision, so over-commit fails at the source instead of after.
        </li>
        <li>
          Central engine for order types (VMs, block storage, security groups, HSM). That cut post-provisioning failure orders by about 40% in the numbers we tracked.
        </li>
        <li>
          Async order-processing pipeline on RabbitMQ for compute, storage, and networking across hybrid cloud.
        </li>
        <li>
          OPS logging with end-to-end traces on provisioning failures. Incident close time dropped about 60% on the paths we instrumented.
        </li>
        <li>
          Disaster recovery: REST API work and asynchronous replication workflows with infrastructure teams. Not a one-person feature; I was a core contributor.
        </li>
        <li>
          Scheduled PostgreSQL to Oracle sync so order state (Postgres) and provisioning state (Oracle) do not drift.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-faint">
        Java 17 · Spring Boot · Spring MVC · PostgreSQL · Oracle · RabbitMQ · Redis · Hibernate/JPA · REST · Maven · Linux
      </p>

      <h2 class="title pt-4 text-ink">Stack</h2>
      <p>
        Java is the main language. Spring Boot, Spring MVC, Spring Data JPA, Hibernate. PostgreSQL, Oracle, Redis, RabbitMQ. Docker, Kubernetes, Maven, Git. A lot of async processing and event-driven work.
      </p>

      <h2 class="title pt-4 text-ink">In public</h2>
      <p>
        Season 1 of the course, plus a bitmask permission engine you can hit with curl. That is the list for now.
      </p>

      <h2 class="title pt-4 text-ink">Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>
        Earlier: Kavach, an Android SOS app (Java, XML, Firebase). Gold medal at Anveshana 2023; shortlisted for the Government of India Tech Innovation Awards. It is not a curriculum build and it is not listed under Projects.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a>
        {" · "}
        <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>
        {" · "}
        <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>
        {" · "}
        <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={SITE.youtube}>YouTube</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="card h-fit min-w-0 p-6">
      <p class="caption text-faint">Now</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">Filming Season 1 · Memory &amp; Low-Level</p>
      <p class="caption mt-6 text-faint">Mail</p>
      <a class="mt-2 block text-sm text-accent hover:underline break-all" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
      <p class="caption mt-6 text-faint">Socials</p>
      <div class="mt-3 min-w-0">
        <SocialIcons />
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
